Let $F_v$ be a nonarchimedean local field of characteristic zero, with residue field $\mathbb F_q$, and let $\mathcal D$ be a central division algebra over $F_v$ of odd degree $n\geq3$. Put $S_v=\mathop{\mathrm{SL}}_1(\mathcal D)$. Reduction induces an isomorphism $$S_v/\overline{[S_v,S_v]}
 \simeq T_v:=\ker\bigl(N_{\mathbb F_{q^n}/\mathbb F_q}:
                       \mathbb F_{q^n}^\times\to\mathbb F_q^\times\bigr).$$ Moreover, $$\overline{[\mathcal D^\times,\mathcal D^\times]}=S_v.$$ If an element of $\mathcal D^\times$ has reduced-norm valuation $r$, its action on $T_v$ is $\sigma^r$, where $\sigma:z\mapsto z^{q^h}$ for some $h$ relatively prime to $n$.

For every finite nonabelian simple group $\mathcal F$ there is a nonempty proper conjugacy-invariant subset $\mathcal S\subset\mathcal F$ with the following property. If $W\in\mathcal S$, $Z\notin\mathcal S$, and $WZ=ZW$, then it is impossible that $$\label{eq:palette-obstruction}
 ZW\in C(B)(ZW^{-1})C(BZ^2)
 \qquad\text{for every }B\in\mathcal F,$$ where $C(B)=C_{\mathcal F}(B)$ denotes the centralizer of $B$ in $\mathcal F$.

The group $G(k)$ contains an involution geometrically conjugate to $\alpha^\vee(-1)$ for a root $\alpha$. Its centralizer $H$ is connected semisimple of type $A_1A_5$, and its simply connected covering has geometric form $$\label{eq:e6-centralizer-cover}
 \pi:\mathop{\mathrm{SL}}_2\times\mathop{\mathrm{SL}}_6\longrightarrow H_{\bar k},
 \qquad \ker\pi=\langle(-I_2,-I_6)\rangle.$$
